What is Cabin Surveillance System?
Cabin surveillance system is a composite technology platform that combines high resolution cameras, robust data storage, network connectivity and advanced analytics software to capture and analyse every activity within an aircraft cabin. The system provides continuous video feeds to both on board crew and downstream operations centers, enabling rapid incident detection, real time decision support and post flight evidence collection.
The industry definition extends beyond simple video capture; it includes multimodal sensors such as seat belt and facial recognition modules, and cloud enabled storage that satisfies stringent aviation data privacy requirements. As airlines increasingly adopt predictive maintenance models, cabin surveillance data has become a critical input for condition monitoring and proactive crew management.
